<html>
<head>
<title>(blow-cl)</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="/style.css">
</head>
<body>
<h1>(blow-cl)</h1>
<p>A Lisp web application framework for the JVM &mdash; the 2009 BLOW idea on a 2026 toolchain.</p>
<hr>

<h2>Congratulations!</h2>
<p>You're running <b>blow-cl</b>. This page is an <code>index.blo</code> template: plain HTML with embedded Common Lisp, executed per request by cl-emb on ABCL.</p>

<% (multiple-value-bind (second minute hour date month year)
       (get-decoded-time)
     (format *standard-output*
             "<p>It is now ~2,'0d:~2,'0d:~2,'0d on ~d-~2,'0d-~2,'0d (server time).</p>"
             hour minute second year month date)) %>

<p>Also try <a href="/hello">/hello</a>, a compiled cl-who page with per-session state.</p>

<h3>Lineage</h3>
<p>blow-cl is a rewrite of <a href="https://github.com/atgreen/blow">BLOW</a> by Anthony Green (2007&ndash;2010), LGPLv3. Winstone became Jetty, the Makefile became Gradle, jfli became ABCL's native interop, and the vendored 2009 Lisp libraries became Quicklisp dependencies.</p>
</body>
</html>
